1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Erhard_Areschoug '''Johan Erhard Areschoug'''] (Johannes Erhard Areschoug, Philos. Doctor, Botanices et Oeconomiae) was a Swedish botanist who was a native of Göteborg. He was a
2 CONC  member of the [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arreskow_(sl%C3%A4kt%29 Arreskow] family (in Swedish). His first name is sometimes recorded as "John".
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He studied natural''' sciences at the University of Lund, where in 1838 he earned his doctorate in philosophy. In 1859 he succeeded [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elias_Magnus_Fries '''Elias Magnus Fries'''] as professor of bot
2 CONC any at the University of Uppsala, a position he maintained until 1876. In 1851, he was elected a member of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Swedish_Academy_of_Sciences Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Areschoug performed''' extensive field studies of Scandinavian cryptogams, being remembered for his work in the field of phycology. The red algae genus Areschougia from the family Areschougiaceae is named in his honor. The stan
2 CONC dard author abbreviation Aresch. is used to indicate this person as the author when citing a botanical name.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Selected publications===
2 CONT * Symbolae Algarum rar. Florae scandinavicae (1838).
2 CONT * Iconographia phycologica (1847).
2 CONT * Phyceae scanidnavicae marinae (1850).
2 CONT * Observationes phycologicae (1883).
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=18781 Riksarkivet SBL]
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/215870245 FindAgrave]
